2840. Check if Strings Can be Made Equal With Operations II
Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/check-if-strings-can-be-made-equal-with-operations-ii/description/?envType=daily-question&envId=2026-03-30
You are given two strings s1 and s2, both of length n, consisting of lowercase English letters.

You can apply the following operation on any of the two strings any number of times:

Choose any two indices i and j such that i < j and the difference j - i is even, then swap the two characters at those indices in the string.
Return true if you can make the strings s1 and s2 equal, and false otherwise.\

Example 1:
Input: s1 = "abcdba", s2 = "cabdab"
Output: true
Explanation: We can apply the following operations on s1:
- Choose the indices i = 0, j = 2. The resulting string is s1 = "cbadba".
- Choose the indices i = 2, j = 4. The resulting string is s1 = "cbbdaa".
- Choose the indices i = 1, j = 5. The resulting string is s1 = "cabdab" = s2.

Example 2:
Input: s1 = "abe", s2 = "bea"
Output: false
Explanation: It is not possible to make the two strings equal.

#Intuition:
1️ Swaps are only allowed within same parity indices
2️ So string splits into 2 groups: even & odd
3️ You can freely rearrange inside each group
4️ So compare sorted characters of even positions
5️ And compare sorted characters of odd positions


class Solution {
    public boolean checkStrings(String s1, String s2) {
        int n=s1.length();
        int n1=(n+1)/2;
        int n2=n/2;
    
        char []ch1=new char[n1];
        char []ch2=new char[n1];
        char []ch3=new char[n2];
        char []ch4=new char[n2];
        int e=0,o=0;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(i%2==0){
                ch1[e]=s1.charAt(i);
                ch2[e]=s2.charAt(i);
                e++;
            }else{
                ch3[o]=s1.charAt(i);
                ch4[o]=s2.charAt(i);
                o++;
            }
        }
        Arrays.sort(ch1);
        Arrays.sort(ch2);
        Arrays.sort(ch3);
        Arrays.sort(ch4);
        System.out.println(ch1);
        return (Arrays.equals(ch1,ch2) && Arrays.equals(ch3,ch4));
    }
}
